# JOURNEY · bait by use: a Bait is a stack of CASTS_PER_BUFF (5) casts, spent by every cast it helps,
# a human's or a rig's, and never by the clock. The player buys three Baits, drinks one into a buff,
# and lets an Angler Rig fish for it: the rig is Rod's coil listening to its own output, so its cast
# rises every other stage and it spends one Bait from the bag per cast, 30 to 60 game seconds apart.
# The status bar shows the stack and what is left of it; after a few landed casts it has counted down.
# Rod's panel walks by count: listens, drives, threshold, cast.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/grow-a-matrixtank.play
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Inverter Coil" Fabric
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Angler Rig" Hands
include scenes/take-a-fish.play botfish rod

run /shop
key enter
select Bait
key enter
key right 2
expect < 3 >
key enter
key esc
key esc
absent Price/unit

run /consume bait
expect baiting
expect 5
snap one Bait is one stack of five casts
tick 300
expect 5 casts
snap a paused rod spends nothing, however long the buff sits

run /consume inverter coil
key enter
run /consume angler rig
key enter
absent to the botfishes

run /fps 1
run /program "Rod"
type go
key down
type go
key down 2
expect threshold
type go
key enter
absent listens

tick 130
absent 5 casts
expect baiting
snap the rig's landed casts counted the stack down
